ity":0.0,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":0.0,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":11.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.14073375131381693,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.4236663246986407,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.01181,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":7.9,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Tango Therapeutics, Inc., a precision oncology company, focuses on the discovery and development of drugs in defined patient populations with unmet medical need. The company develops methylthioadenosine -cooperative protein arginine methyltransferase 5 (PRMT5) inhibitors, including TNG462, which is in Phase 1/2 clinical trial for treating pancreatic and lung cancer; and TNG456, a brain-penetrant PRMT5 inhibitor for the treatment of glioblastoma. It is developing TNG260, a co-repressor of repressor element-1 silencing transcription inhibitor to reverse the immune evasion effect of serine-threonine kinase (STK) 11 loss-of-function mutations to treat lung cancer. The company was founded in 2017 and is headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Malte  Peters M.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $148,315 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 137 people. Revenue per employee of $455K ranks in the above the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 14%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $193K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Tango Therapeutics, Inc. is a mid-cap healthcare business with a $4.3B market cap on $62M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +36% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -3614% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $140M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at +9.4% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 42% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (28.8% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Healthcare peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Operating margins 178% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Accruals running hot at +9.4% of assets \u2014 earnings quality bears watching","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 193% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Tango Therapeutics (NASDAQ:TNGX) & Lakefront Biotherapeutics American Depositary Shares (NASDAQ:LKFT) Head-To-Head Contrast","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/tango-therapeutics-nasdaqtngx-lakefront-biotherapeutics-american-depositary-shares-nasdaqlkft-head-to-head-contrast.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794604518.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.928,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Tango Therapeutics, Inc. $TNGX Position Cut by Pictet Asset Management Holding SA","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/tango-therapeutics-inc-tngx-position-cut-by-pictet-asset-management-holding-sa.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794565643.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.896,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Tango Therapeutics (NASDAQ:TNGX) Stock Gets Price Target Trim from HC Wainwright","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/1